1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Most resilience plans can tell you
a backup exists.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:10,000
They cannot tell you whether the critical
workload will actually recover in time.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,900
This is Systemic Resilience Copilot.

4
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:19,100
Apertus turns a normal-language recovery
scenario into structured evidence.

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:24,000
Deterministic rules then identify the first
binding or unresolved condition justified by that evidence.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,800
In this synthetic case, Northstar Bank
has a sixty-minute tolerance.

7
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:33,100
The recovery route is outside
the primary failure domain,

8
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,000
supports the same workload,
and has been tested.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,900
But observed recovery takes
ninety-five minutes.

10
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,200
Apertus extracts only the facts
that are explicitly stated,

11
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,600
and the host validates them
before the rules run.

12
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,000
Missing downstream evidence remains UNKNOWN.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,100
Now the decision is simple and traceable.

14
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,300
Recovery independence passes,
but execution fails.

15
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:05,700
Ninety-five minutes is longer than sixty,
so the first binding state is S five red, B two.

16
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:09,200
The next action is specific:
repair execution and retest.

17
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,000
We do not jump to a downstream
capacity conclusion.

18
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,200
Now Apertus challenges and explains
the already-fixed decision.

19
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:23,400
It shows why the conclusion follows
and what evidence is still missing,

20
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:29,000
but it cannot override the deterministic state.
AI explains. Rules decide.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,600
We apply only that narrow fix
and rerun the same workload.

22
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:39,400
Recovery now completes
in forty-five minutes.

23
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:44,400
S five passes, but the product
does not declare full resilience.

24
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:50,000
The next unresolved state becomes visible:
S six UNKNOWN — establish simultaneous-demand evidence.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,800
Only then do we open the systemic lens.
Three synthetic institutions may need the same recovery fabric.

26
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:03,900
S four and S five pass, but assured capacity,
priority and coordination remain UNKNOWN.

27
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:08,100
The result is S seven UNKNOWN.

28
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:11,700
Next: measure capacity
and obtain entitlement evidence.

29
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:15,000
A shared recovery resource
is not proof of a shortage.

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,500
Evidence becomes a decision,
and the decision becomes an action.

31
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:24,000
When the evidence stops,
the inference stops.
